================================================================================
                         aniShows - TODO / Roadmap
================================================================================

Legend:
  ✅ = Done    🔧 = Partially done    ⬜ = Not started

================================================================================
CURRENT STRENGTHS
================================================================================
- Full-stack architecture (Django + React + PostgreSQL + Redis) ✅
- JWT + Google OAuth authentication ✅
- Celery automation for anime data sync (trending, seasonal, airing) ✅
- Clean component architecture with TanStack Query ✅
- Security (rate limiting 12+ throttle classes, CSP, XSS prevention, audit logs) ✅
- Content-based recommendation engine (genre/studio/type similarity) ✅
- Import/Export (MAL API, MAL XML, AniList import; JSON + MAL XML export) ✅
- Social features (follow system, activity feed, friends watching) ✅
- Forums with threaded replies (10 depth levels) ✅
- Notifications (in-app + web push + email) ✅
- Gamification (badges, points, reputation) 🔧
- Admin panel with Celery task management, user/content moderation ✅
- Monitoring (Prometheus + Grafana dashboards + Sentry) ✅
- Automated backups (daily + weekly, DB + MinIO) ✅
- CI/CD pipeline (GitHub Actions → GHCR → EC2) ✅
- PWA with offline support and service worker caching ✅
- Image optimization (WebP thumbnails, lazy loading, on-demand resize) ✅
- API docs (drf-spectacular / OpenAPI) ✅
- Frontend testing (Vitest) ✅
- TypeScript migration ✅
- Elasticsearch for advanced search + fuzzy matching ✅

================================================================================
PRIORITY 1 — CRITICAL (Scale & Retention Blockers)
================================================================================

1. Real-Time Features via WebSockets ⬜
   Currently all interactions are request/response. No WebSocket layer exists.
   - Add Django Channels with Redis channel layer
   - Real-time notifications (eliminate polling)
   - Live forum thread updates (new posts appear without refresh)
   - "Currently watching" presence indicators
   - Live anime discussion during airing episodes
   Impact: Massive UX improvement, key for engagement and retention

2. Collaborative Filtering for Recommendations ⬜
   Current engine is content-based only (genre/studio similarity).
   - User-user collaborative filtering (users who liked X also liked Y)
   - Item-item collaborative filtering
   - Hybrid approach combining collaborative + content-based signals
   - Factor in user ratings, completion rate, watch time
   - Cold-start handling for new users (onboarding quiz / preference picker)
   Impact: Much better recommendation accuracy, core differentiator

3. Horizontal Scaling Readiness ⬜
   Single EC2 instance, sync Gunicorn workers, no load balancing.
   - Switch Gunicorn to async workers (uvicorn/hypercorn via ASGI)
   - Add health-check-based auto-scaling (AWS ASG or similar)
   - Database read replicas for heavy read traffic
   - Redis Cluster or Sentinel for HA
   - CDN for static assets and images (CloudFront / Cloudflare)
   - Connection pooling (pgBouncer)
   - Separate Celery workers by queue on dedicated instances
   Impact: Required to serve >1000 concurrent users reliably

4. Comprehensive Backend Test Suite ⬜
   Frontend has Vitest tests but backend test coverage is minimal.
   - Unit tests for all services (recommendation, import, export, auth, security)
   - Integration tests for API endpoints (DRF APITestCase)
   - Celery task tests with mocked brokers
   - Factory Boy fixtures for test data
   - Coverage enforcement in CI (target: 70%+)
   - Load/stress testing with Locust or k6
   Impact: Prevents regressions, enables confident refactoring

5. Internationalization (i18n / l10n) ⬜
   Only an i18n URL route exists, no actual translations.
   - Backend: Django's i18n framework, mark all user-facing strings
   - Frontend: react-i18next with lazy-loaded locale bundles
   - Start with: English, Japanese, Spanish, Portuguese, French
   - RTL support for Arabic
   - Locale-aware date/number formatting
   - User language preference in profile settings
   Impact: Opens platform to global anime community (massive TAM expansion)

================================================================================
PRIORITY 2 — HIGH (User Experience & Engagement)
================================================================================

6. Watch Parties / Shared Viewing ⬜
   - Synchronized episode watching with friends (countdown / play sync)
   - Real-time chat during watch sessions
   - Invite links, scheduled watch parties
   - Integration with streaming service timestamps
   Impact: Strong social hook, differentiator from MAL/AniList

7. Enhanced Discovery & Browsing ⬜
   - Mood-based filtering ("happy", "action-packed", "emotional")
   - Duration-based filtering ("30 min episodes", "movie-length")
   - "Because you watched X" carousels on homepage
   - Seasonal popularity rankings (community votes)
   - Staff/voice actor filmography browsing
   - "Hidden gems" section (high-rated, low-popularity)
   - Anime comparison tool (side-by-side stats/ratings)
   Impact: Better content discovery = more engagement

8. User-Generated Lists & Collections ⬜
   - Custom public lists ("Best Mecha Anime", "Top 10 Romance")
   - List sharing with unique URLs
   - Community voting on lists
   - Featured/curated lists on homepage
   - List templates (seasonal watchlist, genre deep-dive)
   Impact: Content creation keeps users engaged and drives SEO traffic

9. Enhanced Review System ⬜
   - Review drafts (auto-save)
   - Rich media in reviews (screenshots, GIFs)
   - Review templates (structured vs. freeform)
   - "Most helpful" reviewer leaderboard
   - Review reporting/moderation queue improvements
   - Anime rating breakdown visualization (radar chart)
   Impact: Higher quality UGC, more community value

10. Advanced Profile & Stats ⬜
    - Anime compatibility score between two users
    - Year-in-review annual summary (like Spotify Wrapped)
    - Genre evolution timeline (how tastes change over time)
    - Watch pace analytics (episodes/week trends)
    - Milestone celebrations (100th anime, 1000 episodes)
    - Profile themes/customization (colors, layout)
    - Public API for user stats (embeddable widgets for blogs/Discord)
    Impact: Users love stats, drives sharing and return visits

11. Gamification Expansion 🔧
    Badges exist but watch streaks and achievement system are thin.
    - Watch streaks with streak freeze (like Duolingo)
    - Daily/weekly challenges ("Watch 3 episodes of a new genre")
    - XP system with levels
    - Seasonal events with limited-time badges
    - Leaderboards (most active, best reviewer, longest streak)
    - Collectible profile frames/borders
    Impact: Daily engagement driver

================================================================================
PRIORITY 3 — MEDIUM (Platform Maturity)
================================================================================

12. Mobile App (React Native) ⬜
    PWA exists but native app provides better experience.
    - React Native with shared API layer
    - Push notifications (native, not web push)
    - Offline anime list access
    - Barcode/QR scanning for physical anime media
    - Widget for "currently watching" on home screen
    Impact: Mobile users are majority of traffic for entertainment apps

13. Content Moderation & Trust System ⬜
    - User trust levels (new → regular → trusted → moderator)
    - Community flagging with automatic escalation thresholds
    - Automated content filtering (profanity, spam detection)
    - Mod tools: shadow ban, slow mode, IP-based restrictions
    - Appeal system for moderation actions
    - Mod activity dashboard with metrics
    Impact: Required at scale to maintain community quality

14. Accessibility (a11y) Audit & Fixes 🔧
    Some ARIA attributes exist but coverage is inconsistent.
    - Full WCAG 2.1 AA compliance audit
    - Consistent ARIA labels on all interactive elements
    - Keyboard navigation for all features (carousels, modals, drag-drop)
    - Screen reader testing (NVDA, VoiceOver)
    - Color contrast validation across all themes
    - Reduced motion support (prefers-reduced-motion)
    - Focus management for route changes and modals
    Impact: Legal compliance, larger audience, better UX for everyone

15. Streaming Service Integration ⬜
    - Show where an anime is available to stream (Crunchyroll, Netflix, etc.)
    - Deep links to specific anime on streaming platforms
    - Availability by region
    - Price comparison across platforms
    - "New on [Platform]" sections
    Impact: Answers the #1 question users have: "where can I watch this?"

16. Email & Engagement Automation ⬜
    Email service exists but only for transactional emails.
    - Weekly digest: new episodes for watchlist, trending in your genres
    - Re-engagement emails (inactive 7/14/30 days)
    - New season preview recommendations
    - "Your friend started watching X" emails
    - Email preference center with granular controls
    - Unsubscribe handling with feedback
    Impact: Brings users back, standard for any platform at scale

17. API Rate Limiting & Public API ⬜
    Internal API exists but no public developer API.
    - API key management for third-party developers
    - OAuth2 for third-party app authorization
    - Public API documentation portal
    - Rate limit tiers (free: 100/hr, premium: 1000/hr)
    - Webhook support for list changes, new episodes
    Impact: Ecosystem growth, third-party apps, integrations

================================================================================
PRIORITY 4 — NICE TO HAVE (Polish & Differentiation)
================================================================================

18. AI-Powered Features ⬜
    - Natural language anime search ("anime like Steins;Gate but more romance")
    - AI-generated review summaries (aggregate sentiment from all reviews)
    - Automatic tagging/categorization of user reviews
    - Chatbot for anime recommendations
    Impact: Modern UX, marketing differentiator

19. Monetization Infrastructure ⬜
    - Premium tier (advanced stats, custom themes, ad-free, early features)
    - Stripe/payment integration
    - Streaming service affiliate links with revenue tracking
    - Sponsored recommendations (clearly labeled)
    - Donation/tip system for top reviewers
    Impact: Revenue generation for sustainability

20. Performance & Infrastructure Polish ⬜
    - Database query optimization (N+1 detection, EXPLAIN analysis)
    - Redis memory optimization (key expiry audit, memory policy)
    - Frontend bundle size audit and reduction
    - Server-side rendering (SSR) or static generation for SEO pages
    - Edge caching for API responses (Cloudflare Workers / Lambda@Edge)
    - Database partitioning for activity/logs tables
    - Automated performance regression testing in CI
    Impact: Faster load times, lower infrastructure costs

21. Advanced Forum Features ⬜
    - Polls in threads
    - Anime-specific discussion boards (auto-created per anime)
    - Episode discussion threads (auto-created on air date)
    - User reputation/karma in forums
    - Rich embeds (anime cards, user profiles) in posts
    - Spoiler tagging system with granular episode spoiler levels
    Impact: Richer community interaction

22. Data Analytics & Insights ⬜
    - Public site-wide stats page (total users, anime tracked, reviews)
    - Seasonal anime popularity predictions
    - Genre trend analytics over time
    - Community taste mapping (clustering visualization)
    - Admin: user cohort analysis, retention funnels, churn prediction
    Impact: Interesting for users, valuable for product decisions

23. Desktop Enhancements ⬜
    - Keyboard-driven power user mode (vim-like navigation)
    - Customizable homepage layout (drag-and-drop widgets)
    - Browser extension for anime detection on streaming sites
    - Discord bot integration (update list from Discord)
    Impact: Power user retention

================================================================================
TECHNICAL DEBT & MAINTENANCE
================================================================================

24. Code Quality ⬜
    - Deduplicate admin_views.py between animes/ and users/ apps
    - Extract shared serializer logic into proper mixin library
    - Standardize error response format across all endpoints
    - Add structured logging (replace print statements)
    - OpenTelemetry tracing for distributed request tracking

25. Security Hardening ⬜
    - Regular dependency vulnerability scanning (Dependabot + Snyk)
    - API input validation audit (fuzzing)
    - Session management improvements (concurrent session limits)
    - 2FA support (TOTP / authenticator apps)
    - Security.txt and responsible disclosure policy
    - Penetration testing schedule

26. DevOps & Reliability ⬜
    - Blue-green or canary deployments (currently rolling restart)
    - Database migration safety checks (no-downtime migrations)
    - Automated rollback on failed health checks
    - Staging environment matching production
    - Infrastructure as Code (Terraform / Pulumi)
    - Log aggregation (ELK stack or Loki)
    - Uptime monitoring with status page (public)

